 ## Do not touch
 Tiers 0 to 3 and their order; the fence over `.agent/` that a self-use run carries (DECISION
 amend0926-decisions-selfuse D4); the ratchet's rule that the count may only go down.
+
+## Built State (F291, 2026-09-29)
+
+What exists on disk at the close of F291, built on `feature/f291-self-use-sources-v2`, cut from
+`main` at `aa5defde`. Every DECISION named lives in `.agent/decisions.md`; every round's verdict in
+`.agent/live_review.md` or, once rotated, its archive.
+
+**T001 — Tier 4, the excused blind handlers.** `packages/orchestration/self_use_generator.py` reads
+the roots and the mark pattern `tests/test_ble001_ratchet.py` counts, `EXCUSED_HANDLER_ROOTS` and
+`EXCUSED_HANDLER_MARK`, a test pinning both equal to the ratchet's own. It offers the first mark in
+file-path order and then line order that no queue entry targets; "oldest" is read as first in the
+file, because the generator reads files and never git history. An item's key is the file, the
+ordinal of that line's text among identical lines of the file, and the line itself, so a mark that
+only moves keeps its key and two identical handlers are two items. The job's one task narrows the
+handler, deletes its mark and lowers `MAX_EXCUSED` by one in the same change. The module never spells
+the mark itself: its text is composed from `EXCUSE_MARK_WORDS`, and a test holds that no line of the
+module matches the ratchet's pattern (DECISION F291 D1).
+
+**T002 — Tier 5, the test-less modules.** The same module offers the first module, in path order
+under `packages/` and then `apps/cli/`, that is not a package's `__init__.py`, defines a top-level
+function or class, and whose dotted name no `import` statement in any file under `tests/` binds. Its
+job names the functions and classes to test, the public ones or every one when none is public, since
+all fifteen such modules measured at the claim define only private names, and asks for a test file
+named after the module. Both tiers come after Tier 3, Tier 4 first; both read files under
+`default_source_root()`, which `generate_self_use_item` and `generate_and_append_if_empty` accept as
+`source_root`; both screen what they copy with `RETIRED_WORD`; and both raise
+`SelfUseGenerationError` on a file they cannot read or parse (DECISION F291 D1).
+
+**T003 — the requirement.** `tests/orchestration/test_self_use_generator.py` holds that three requests
+on a queue dry for tiers 0 to 3 give three different items and then none, and
+`tests/orchestration/test_self_use_runner.py` that the first of three such items, a Tier 4 item, runs
+through `run_next_self_use_item` to the approval gate under the default budget, its one task applied
+to the job's own workspace and its calls inside the default provider-call cap (DECISION F291 D2). The
+closure's own self-use run is the live reading of the same clause. `docs/system/self-use-track-v1.md`
+and precondition 6 of `docs/roadmap/STATUS_closure_protocol.md` describe the two new sources.
